cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this attribution contract, its within-panel stability audit, or its public artifact, cite the manuscript. No archival release (git tag plus DOI) exists yet: this tree is a v0.1.1 release candidate. The source code is MIT-licensed, code only; the ICEWS-derived aggregate results are not MIT."
title: "Actor-role components of dyadic event forecasts: exact attribution, near-collinearity, and a within-panel stability audit"
abstract: >-
  Public artifact and L0-L2 verification release for the actor-role
  attribution contract of this manuscript, together with a within-panel
  stability audit. The contract fixes feature ownership, unit and sign
  before results, so every logistic forecast carries an exact group-additive
  decomposition into source-role, target-role, dyad and non-actor groups. It
  is a design convention and audit, not a new estimator: the decomposition
  is the logistic identity and coincides with linear SHAP under a
  training-mean background. The release is one paper path, not a reusable
  framework, and is executable at L0-L2 only (read the frozen aggregates,
  verify their hashes and contracts, re-render the notebooks). The
  restricted 50-refit audit code and all ICEWS inputs are not redistributed;
  row-level predictions and labels are withheld. The confirmatory evaluation
  is a pre-registered, one-shot, unit-fresh 20% dyad holdout; it is
  retrospective, not time-fresh. The stability audit is provisional,
  holdout-row-excluded and based on 50 dyad-cluster bootstrap refits; it is
  not a holdout-side stability test. The public experiment scripts are a
  five-seed preview of the audit method and do not regenerate the 50-refit
  holdout-row-excluded aggregates. No general claim is made about graph
  features, persistence or any corpus beyond this panel. Source code is
  MIT-licensed; ICEWS-derived aggregate results are not MIT and remain under
  the ICEWS research-and-teaching terms. This is a v0.1.1 release candidate:
  the v0.1.1 git tag, the DOI and the author metadata (individual names,
  affiliations, ORCIDs) are pending.
# Author metadata pending: no individual author names, affiliations or ORCIDs
# have been supplied. This collective label is a placeholder, not an ORCID claim.
authors:
  - name: "LAGS-1 authors"
version: "0.1.1"
license: other-open
keywords:
